[{"name":"fabricekalvanda/PartyPlaning","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/PartyPlaning","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"This program is set to arrange the seating at a particular awards ceremony. Your job is to rearrange the names in various orders using loops and linked lists so that the client will be able to choose amongst different options per their request. ","topics":[],"score":227160,"global_rank":122438},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/OrderTracker","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/OrderTracker","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"I run a restaurant called \u201cTina\u2019s Palace.\u201d At my restaurant, I take orders on a first come first serve basis. However, I track the orders at the end of the day on a last in first out basis. For example, if I have 10 customers whose orders are. The console will introduce the user and prompt the user to enter X number of orders. It will then print out the list of orders in ascending and descending order i.e. using a stack and queue.   If the customer enters \u201cQUIT\u201d the outro will be printed and both lists will be printed to the console.","topics":[],"score":227160,"global_rank":122439},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/SeachAndSort","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/SeachAndSort","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"Given a list of numbers by the user, this program will find the element the user is searching for.","topics":[],"score":227160,"global_rank":122440},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/shapes","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/shapes","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"I have multiple shapes. Each shape does something different depending on what it is.","topics":[],"score":227160,"global_rank":122441},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/quilts","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/quilts","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"I have a business that sells quilts of the same pattern, but different sizes depending on the customers needs. A customer is able to request a quilt with this pattern as big as they want.","topics":[],"score":227160,"global_rank":122442},{"name":"fabricekalvanda/diceGame","owner":"fabricekalvanda","html_url":"https://github.com/fabricekalvanda/diceGame","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"I have 2 die, 6 sided each I start the game and print the intro  \u201cHey! Welcome to Tina\u2019s Dice Game.\u201d \u201cLet\u2019s start!\u201d The computer randomly generates what side of the die is chosen (for each die) I then add both of the random numbers together  I then print  Dice 1 = (the random number I got)  Dice 2 = (the random number I got) Depending on what number I get, something different is printed to the screen If I get an even number  I print \u201cI got (value of dice 1) and (value of dice 2)!\u201d  I print \u201cEvens are better than odds!\u201d If I get an odd number I print \u201cI got (value of dice 1) and (value of dice 2)!\u201d  I print \u201cOdds are still cool!\u201d At the end, I ask the user if they want to play again If the answer is \u201cYES\u201d  I \u201cthrow\u201d the die again and repeat the printing process If the answer is anything but YES (case-sensitive) I end the game and print the outro  \u201cThe number of times the dice was thrown is: (value of times dice is thrown)\u201d \u201cNice game!\u201d \u201cThanks for playing, Come play again soon!\u201d\u2028","topics":[],"score":227160,"global_rank":122443},{"name":"GregBahm/PokerVis","owner":"GregBahm","html_url":"https://github.com/GregBahm/PokerVis","stars":0,"forks":1,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"Visualize the win probabilities of poker hands","to